From 70221358a62cc080f3592d01da059e7980018382 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:47:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4 dynarmic: predicated A32 instructions in place, float
 compares straight to the flags, per-site indirect jumps

inline_conditional_instructions (A32; on in Eden): a conditional ARM instruction in the middle of
a block (cond_state None, not Thumb) is translated in place. TranslateArm then checks its IR:
register writes other than PC, writes of D/S registers and of all four flags become
ConditionalSelect32/64/NZCV of the new value and the value read before the instruction (the
flags' through a new A32GetCpsrNZCV, the stored host-format word; a CPSR reader for the get/set
pass). Anything else (memory, partial flag writes as TST and MOVS, branches, exceptions, floating
point or vector operations, which must not touch FPSCR's cumulative bits when not executed) has
its IR undone, latest first, and the block ends before it as before. Before, each such
instruction split its code into three linked blocks.

A32FpscrNZCVForwarding: VMRS APSR_nzcv after VCMP in the same block stores the compare's NZCV
(host format) straight to the CPSR instead of through FPSCR's ARM format and back. FPCompare's
bits above 15 are not zero; every reader of cpsr_nzcv uses only AH and AL or masks (as A64's
FCMP already relies on).

inline_fast_dispatch (A32 and A64; on in Eden): a FastDispatchHint terminal hashes into the fast
dispatch table and jumps in its own block (the miss path still shared), so each site's indirect
jump is predicted on its own, as inline_rsb_pop does for returns. Two alternating single-target
call sites, 100,000 calls, callgrind's branch simulator: indirect mispredicts 106,401 -> 6,405.

A32 GetCpsrNZCV stubs for the arm64 (real) and riscv64 backends.

Host harness (game-like image, PS4 CPU features): A32 470k -> 449k host instructions a frame
(03.88: 632k). Differential tests, old build vs new with every option on, with and without
fastmem: gen7.py (now also conditional compares, VFP moves and adds, VCMP/VCMPE + VMRS before
branches and conditional instructions, indirect calls) and gen.py/gen3.py/gen4.py for A32;
gen8.py (now with BLR) for A64. With every option on: 1,202 gen7 programs and 451 gen8 programs,
all equal; earlier rounds with the options added one by one: 3,016 more A32 programs, equal. A
generator bug (Thumb indirect calls into ARM state) made 103 Thumb programs fail on the old and
new builds alike; fixed, those 103 seeds pass with and without fastmem.
